{"term":"efficient","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:94ade0eb6770a24224","definition":"Making good, thorough, or careful use of resources; not consuming extra. Especially, making good use of time or energy.","example":"An efficient process would automate all the routine work.","pos":"adj","synonyms":["lean","businesslike"],"antonyms":["inefficient","prodigal","uneconomical"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["cost-efficient","ecoefficient","efficient cause","efficient frontier","efficiently","efficient market hypothesis","efficientness","energy-efficient","energy efficient","equiefficient","hyperefficient","Kaldor-Hicks efficient","nonefficient","subefficient","superefficient","tax-efficient","ultraefficient"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/efficient#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:87f2931b01357d8a1e","definition":"Expressing the proportion of consumed energy that was successfully used in a process; the ratio of useful output to total input.","example":"The motor is only 20% efficient at that temperature.","pos":"adj","synonyms":["economical","efficacious","efficient","potent"],"antonyms":["inefficient","prodigal","uneconomical"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["cost-efficient","ecoefficient","efficient cause","efficient frontier","efficiently","efficient market hypothesis","efficientness","energy-efficient","energy efficient","equiefficient","hyperefficient","Kaldor-Hicks efficient","nonefficient","subefficient","superefficient","tax-efficient","ultraefficient"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/efficient#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:a96734da5775f64c00","definition":"Causing effects, producing results; bringing into being; initiating change (rare except in philosophical and legal expre